{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"Storage quota monitoring marked done after hard-halt check current status as of 2026-09-22 later evidence reopened it buffer change underway"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"- **2026-09-18**: Bob - Buffer Refactor (Active (Reopened))\\n\\n - *Refactored the disk-usage monitor to allow a 10% buffer above quota, since the reopened hard halt was tripping too aggressively on production-like batches.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2026 09 18 bob buffer refactor activ reopen refactor the disk usag monitor to allow a 10 buffer abov quota sinc the reopen hard halt wa trip too aggress on product like batch\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"id\": \"35710838c33b7c79\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3319131786451376, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11284168377876803, \"vector_similarity\": 0.84308, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1232, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:54\", \"token_count\": 594, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-22\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Storage Quota Management Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:30] Evan**: Starting on storage quota management. We need to keep `cipherdoc` from filling up the disk on these workstations, especially on large batch jobs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:39] Evan**: Implementing a disk-usage monitor loop. It'll check available space before starting any new redaction job.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:41] Alice**: What's the threshold?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:08] Evan**: Going with a hard 500MB floor for now. If free space drops below that, the engine pauses and alerts the user.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:26] Diana**: We also need a way to clear the cache — the `/tmp` folder doesn't always clean up properly after a crash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:41] Evan**: I'll add a purge-cache option and run a sweep on startup too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:44] Evan**: @Bob, can we get a hook in the `FileStreamer` to report current disk usage for the active job?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:30] Bob**: Sure, I'll add a `get_quota_usage()` method to the stream controller.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 22 slack thread storag quota manag design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 04 2026 08 04 09 30 evan start on storag quota manag we need to keep cipherdoc from fill up the disk on these workstat especi on larg batch job 2026 08 04 09 39 evan implement a disk usag monitor loop it ll check avail space befor start ani new redact job 2026 08 04 09 41 alic what s the threshold 2026 08 04 10 08 evan go with a hard 500mb floor for now if free space drop below that the engin paus and alert the user 2026 08 04 10 26 diana we also need a way to clear the cach the tmp folder doesn t alway clean up proper after a crash 2026 08 04 10 41 evan i ll add a purg cach option and run a sweep on startup too 2026 08 04 10 44 evan bob can we get a hook in the filestream to report current disk usag for the activ job 2026 08 04 11 30 bob sure i ll add a get _ quota _ usag method to the stream control\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e0ea928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"id\": \"9a05aa4017f04966\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3180551403377073, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11701161476815333, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7871567, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e0ea928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1088, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:37\", \"token_count\": 344, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-23\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Storage Quota Halt Verification and Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:19] Diana**: Verification done on the disk monitor. Filled the disk with dummy data and confirmed the engine halts writes once it hits the configured 500MB floor. That meets the requirement — calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:46] Evan**: Good. I'll keep an eye on it as we add more features, don't want the threshold logic drifting.\\n\\n**[2026-09-15 10:06] Evan**: Reopening this. Production-like batches are tripping the 500MB hard halt before they've done any useful work — it's too aggressive for how these jobs actually run.\\n\\n**[2026-09-15 10:07] Diana**: Makes sense, a flat cutoff doesn't account for how much a batch has already written before it gets close to the line.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:30] Bob**: Refactored the monitor to use a 10% buffer tolerance above the quota instead of the hard 500MB halt. Root cause was that hard cutoff having no soft buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:31] Diana**: Nice.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:39] Evan**: That should behave a lot better under real batch sizes. I'll re-test against the same production-like batches that tripped it before.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:58] Evan**: Re-tested — no premature halts on the batches that failed before. Looks good.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 23 slack thread storag quota halt verif and reopen channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 06 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 08 06 09 19 diana verif done on the disk monitor fill the disk with dummi data and confirm the engin halt write onc it hit the configur 500mb floor that meet the requir call this done 2026 08 06 09 46 evan good i ll keep an eye on it a we add more featur don t want the threshold logic drift 2026 09 15 10 06 evan reopen this product like batch are trip the 500mb hard halt befor they ve done ani use work it s too aggress for how these job actual run 2026 09 15 10 07 diana make sens a flat cutoff doesn t account for how much a batch ha alreadi written befor it get close to the line 2026 09 18 09 30 bob refactor the monitor to use a 10 buffer toler abov the quota instead of the hard 500mb halt root caus wa that hard cutoff have no soft buffer 2026 09 18 09 31 diana nice 2026 09 18 09 39 evan that should behav a lot better under real batch size i ll re test against the same product like batch that trip it befor 2026 09 18 09 58 evan re test no prematur halt on the batch that fail befor look good\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e913c0348a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"id\": \"532ecaefccbcd3fb\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3073599355268062, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0809777907525803, \"vector_similarity\": 0.83558494, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e913c0348a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1374, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:52\", \"token_count\": 403, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-36\\n\\n# Storage Quota Halt Validation\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2036\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\nConfirm that T022’s disk-usage monitor actually stops further writes once the configured quota is reached—not merely that the loop is running.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-36\\n\\n# Storage Quota Halt Validation\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2036\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nDiana ran the monitor against a configured quota and checked write behavior at the threshold. The monitor halted further writes as required. That initial behavior was accepted as meeting the quota requirement for this pass.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-36\\n\\n# Storage Quota Halt Validation\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2036\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Outcome\\n\\nCompleted. Quota-halt behavior is verified for the configured threshold checked here.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-36\\n\\n# Storage Quota Halt Validation\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2036\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## What remains out of scope\\n\\nThis validation does not redefine the quota policy or introduce a soft buffer above the hard halt. Those questions, if they arise later, are separate from this acceptance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 purpos confirm that t022 s disk usag monitor actual stop further write onc the configur quota is reach not mere that the loop is run sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 verif diana ran the monitor against a configur quota and check write behavior at the threshold the monitor halt further write a requir that initi behavior wa accept a meet the quota requir for this pas sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 outcom complet quota halt behavior is verifi for the configur threshold check here sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 what remain out of scope this valid doe not redefin the quota polici or introduc a soft buffer abov the hard halt those question if they aris later are separ from this accept\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9ba85fe8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"id\": \"94848622d806c45a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29983785047072725, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07733911781532461, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81900156, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9ba85fe8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 834, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:31\", \"token_count\": 328, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-32\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Title**: Halt batch writes when disk quota is hit\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMonitor disk usage during large batch runs and halt writes once a configured quota is reached, to prevent disk exhaustion. The original hard-halt behavior was reopened after proving too aggressive on production-like batches, and the monitor is being refactored to allow a 10% buffer above quota instead of stopping immediately.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-32\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Title**: Halt batch writes when disk quota is hit\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Disk-usage monitor halts writes at the configured quota during batch runs.\\n\\n- Halt behavior tolerates a 10% buffer above quota rather than stopping abruptly at the hard limit.\\n\\n- Refactored monitor no longer trips prematurely on production-like batch sizes.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-32\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Title**: Halt batch writes when disk quota is hit\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMonitor disk usage during large batch runs and halt writes once a configured quota is reached, to prevent disk exhaustion. The original hard-halt behavior was reopened after proving too aggressive on production-like batches, and the monitor is being refactored to allow a 10% buffer above quota instead of stopping immediately.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-32\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Title**: Halt batch writes when disk quota is hit\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-02**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because large batches need a storage quota to prevent disk exhaustion.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 32 sourc id src cu ciph 32 task id ciph 32 titl halt batch write when disk quota is hit status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 02 descript monitor disk usag dure larg batch run and halt write onc a configur quota is reach to prevent disk exhaust the origin hard halt behavior wa reopen after prove too aggress on product like batch and the monitor is be refactor to allow a 10 buffer abov quota instead of stop immedi clickup task ciph 32 sourc id src cu ciph 32 task id ciph 32 titl halt batch write when disk quota is hit status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 02 accept criterion disk usag monitor halt write at the configur quota dure batch run halt behavior toler a 10 buffer abov quota rather than stop abrupt at the hard limit refactor monitor no longer trip prematur on product like batch size clickup task ciph 32 sourc id src cu ciph 32 task id ciph 32 titl halt batch write when disk quota is hit status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 02 descript monitor disk usag dure larg batch run and halt write onc a configur quota is reach to prevent disk exhaust the origin hard halt behavior wa reopen after prove too aggress on product like batch and the monitor is be refactor to allow a 10 buffer abov quota instead of stop immedi clickup task ciph 32 sourc id src cu ciph 32 task id ciph 32 titl halt batch write when disk quota is hit status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 02 activ histori 2026 08 02 alic task creat open open the task becaus larg batch need a storag quota to prevent disk exhaust\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"id\": \"f83d8125c6089091\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2986144417521156, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08323987393159372, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8011551, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1232, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:54\", \"token_count\": 594, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-16\\n\\n# Storage Quota — Disk-Usage Monitor\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2016\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-05 (retrospective of 2026-08-04)\\n\\nLarge batch runs can exhaust local disk if nothing caps write volume. T022 opened to add a storage quota for that reason.\\n\\n## Monitor loop\\n\\nOn 2026-08-04 Evan landed a live disk-usage monitor that watches free space during batch processing and is meant to stop further writes once a configured quota is crossed. The loop is in place; it is not yet a signed-off gate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-16\\n\\n# Storage Quota — Disk-Usage Monitor\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2016\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-05 (retrospective of 2026-08-04)\\n\\nLarge batch runs can exhaust local disk if nothing caps write volume. T022 opened to add a storage quota for that reason.\\n\\n## Still open\\n\\nNobody has yet confirmed that the monitor actually halts writes at the configured threshold. Until that check lands, T022 stays Active.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 16 storag quota disk usag monitor owner evan document key doc 2016 last updat 2026 08 05 retrospect of 2026 08 04 larg batch run can exhaust local disk if noth cap write volum t022 open to add a storag quota for that reason monitor loop on 2026 08 04 evan land a live disk usag monitor that watch free space dure batch process and is meant to stop further write onc a configur quota is cross the loop is in place it is not yet a sign off gate sourc id src gdoc 16 storag quota disk usag monitor owner evan document key doc 2016 last updat 2026 08 05 retrospect of 2026 08 04 larg batch run can exhaust local disk if noth cap write volum t022 open to add a storag quota for that reason still open nobodi ha yet confirm that the monitor actual halt write at the configur threshold until that check land t022 stay activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9c291b88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"id\": \"d1e1b8cab1239d1d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29208472920076434, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0655966131439491, \"vector_similarity\": 0.820557, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9c291b88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 688, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:24\", \"token_count\": 274, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27290936906472585, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11594909866389409, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63915, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25914937824962125, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07749615464231613, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6830069, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25809948624962126, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07749615464231613, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67950726, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughput by rough 10 compar to the expect async speedup becaus worker end up retri serial around the corrupt write recoveri path this is now block further rollout of the async schedul sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 status t037 is block on resolv the manifest write race befor the async schedul can be consid product readi the throughput regress it caus depend direct on how the t026 worker pool s result write is serial\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"188f8e49d969781d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25737800968684454, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06569464240977792, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7046392, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1694, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:51\", \"token_count\": 573, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"Storage quota monitoring marked done after hard-halt check current status as of 2026-09-22 later evidence reopened it buffer change underway\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"As of 2026-09-22, CIPH-32 is **Active (Reopened)**, assigned to Evan—not completed. [SRC-CU-CIPH-32]\n\nIt was reopened on 2026-09-15 after production-like batches hit the 500 MB hard halt before doing useful work; the fixed cutoff was too aggressive and had no soft buffer. [SRC-SLACK-23]\n\nThe monitor is being refactored to tolerate a **10% buffer above quota** instead of stopping at the hard 500 MB limit. Re-testing on the previously failing batch types showed no premature halts, but the task remains reopened while the revised behavior is finalized. [SRC-SLACK-23; SRC-CU-CIPH-32]"}}
